From: KDE1 Revival Project <maintainer@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ntqvariant.h: undef X11's Bool macro around enum Type

KDE 1.1.2 源码普遍先 #include <X11/Xlib.h>（其 #define Bool int）再经
q1compat 链拉入本头——enum Type 中的 Bool 枚举子被 X11 宏二次展开为 int，
产生上百个编译错误；GL/GLX 头在更下游仍依赖 X11 的 Bool 宏。

处理：进入枚举前 #undef Bool，枚举闭合后 #define Bool int 恢复（与 X11
语义一致、幂等；不影响任何 TQt API 名字与语义）。

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [KDE1 Revival 构建环境特有：X11 头先于 TQt 头 include]
Signed-off-by: KDE1 Revival Project Maintainer <maintainer@example.invalid>

--- a/src/kernel/ntqvariant.h
+++ b/src/kernel/ntqvariant.h
@@ -92,6 +92,11 @@
 class TQ_EXPORT TQVariant
 {
 public:
+    // KDE1 Revival: X11/Xlib.h defines `Bool' as a macro (int); it collides
+    // with the enumerator below when X11 headers are included first. Clear
+    // it locally - X11 headers re-define it idempotently if re-included.
+    #undef Bool
+
     enum Type {
 	Invalid,
 	Map,
@@ -129,6 +134,10 @@
 	LongLong,
 	ULongLong
     };
+    // KDE1 Revival: restore X11's Bool macro — client code (GL, X11
+    // helpers) after this header still relies on it; X11 headers also
+    // re-define it idempotently when re-included.
+    #define Bool int
 
     TQVariant();
     ~TQVariant();
